column2:
That was the first part of our journey. 

Now accompany me safely to {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column3:
Det var foerste del av vaar reise.

Foelg meg naa trygt til {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column2:
Enough of these stressful deals.

In the hope that I have not overtaxed your patience please now take me to {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column3:
Nok av disse slitsomme handlene.

I haap om at jeg ikke har satt Deres taalmodighet for hardt paa proeve, foer meg naa til {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column2:
{%V:0E} {%N:0F},

The map was divided into nine pieces among the crew and we spread out in all directions of the compass. No idea where the other pieces are, but I'll keep my ears open.

{%V:0C} {%N:0D}

column3:
{%V:0E} {%N:0F},

Kartet ble delt i ni biter blant mannskapet, og vi spredte oss for alle vinder. Aner ikke hvor de andre bitene er, men jeg skal holde oerene aapne.

{%V:0C} {%N:0D}

column2:
You have fulfilled the mission and shall receive the reward as agreed!

Thank you very much!

{%V:0A} {%N:0C}

column3:
De har fullfoert oppdraget og skal faa den avtalte beloenningen!

Tusen takk!

{%V:0A} {%N:0C}

column2:
Dear {%5:00}{%N:07},

News of the successes of our tranquil town has spread far beyond the town's borders. Now evil powers, full of malice, are planning to rob us of our best by demanding a contribution of the fruit of our hard labour. It has been reported to us that a large army of mercenaries is on its way, and that these fiends will overrun us, murdering, plundering, and burning.Let us take precautionary measures to protect our homes, since we can no longer turn back the bloody storm.

The Town {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Kjaere {%5:00}{%N:07},

Ryktet om vaar fredelige bys fremgang har spredt seg langt utenfor byens grenser. Naa planlegger onde makter, fulle av ondskap, aa fraroeve oss det beste vi har ved aa kreve en del av frukten av vaart harde arbeid. Det er meldt at en stor haer av leiesoldater er paa vei, og at disse djevlene vil velte inn over oss, myrdende, plyndrende og brennende. La oss ta forholdsregler for aa verne vaare hjem, for den blodige stormen kan vi ikke lenger avverge.

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Citizens of  {%t:04}!

Hordes of marauding foreign troops are sweeping through towns, robbing and murdering without mercy. There is no limit to their atrocities. Whether our prayers - that they might refrain from coming to our beautiful town - have been heard, is yet uncertain.
Arm yourselves, reinforce the walls, and stand bravely with your arms!May the walls hold as steadfastly as our courage!

The Town {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Borgere i {%t:04}!

Horder av plyndrende fremmede tropper drar gjennom byene, raner og myrder uten naade. Det finnes ingen grense for deres grusomheter. Om vaare boenner - at de maa skaane vaar vakre by - er blitt hoert, er ennaa uvisst.
Vaepn dere, forsterk murene og staa modig med vaapen i haand! Maatte murene staa like fast som vaart mot!

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Dear Sir,

On their last shore leave, the crew was sitting in a tavern as usual when a drunken sailor bawled out stories about the ship's kobold through the room. He talked about his last ship that was taken by the ship's kobold, and that he was the only one to escape. You know, I do not pay a lot of attention to this superstition but the crew has been a little restless since then. I have got the situation under control and merely wanted to submit a report. 

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Under sin siste landlov satt mannskapet som vanlig paa et vertshus, da en full sjoemann broelte historier om skipsnissen utover rommet. Han fortalte om sitt siste skip, som skipsnissen hadde tatt, og at han var den eneste som slapp unna. De vet at jeg ikke gir mye for denne overtroen, men mannskapet har vaert litt urolig siden. Jeg har situasjonen under kontroll og ville bare avlegge rapport.

Styrmannen paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

These credulous scary-cats have again picked up something about the ship's kobold. This invisible spirit supposedly protects each and every ship, and that should it leave the ship, it would go down with crew and cargo. You know the legend that a ship's kobold shows himself before he leaves a ship. However, these credible sailors now see him grinning from behind every plank. The morale is not very good, that's why you should see about it yourself!

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Disse godtroende reddharene har igjen snappet opp noe om skipsnissen. Denne usynlige aanden skal beskytte hvert eneste skip, og skulle den forlate skipet, gaar det ned med mann og last. De kjenner sagnet om at skipsnissen viser seg foer den forlater et skip. Men naa ser disse godtroende sjoefolkene den glise bak hver planke. Moralen er ikke den beste, derfor boer De se paa saken selv!

Styrmannen paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

This cowardly pack has fled. Here in {%t:08} many sailors have discharged, except for a few courageous ones, due to fear of the ship's kobold. For better or for worse, you will have to engage a new crew before you can set sail again.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Dette feige pakket har flyktet. Her i {%t:08} har mange matroser moenstret av av frykt for skipsnissen, bortsett fra noen faa modige. Enten De vil eller ikke, maa De hyre et nytt mannskap foer vi kan sette seil igjen.

Styrmannen paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

There is talk of unusual sightings near the town of {%t:08}. Several sailors, independent of each other, are said to have seen a ghost ship gliding across the sea and this, despite a calm wind. The crew's heart dropped to the sole of their feet, but they are bravely carrying out their duties. I have doubled the guard to keep things quiet.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Det snakkes om uvanlige syner naer {%t:08}. Flere sjoefolk skal, uavhengig av hverandre, ha sett et spoekelsesskip gli over havet, og det i vindstille. Mannskapet fikk hjertet i halsen, men de gjoer tappert sin plikt. Jeg har doblet vakten for aa holde roen.

Styrmannen paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

The fairy tale of the ship's kobold is again doing the rounds among the crew. I have heard of cases where the crew worked itself into such a state, that the whole ship was put in danger. I will be harder on the sailors than normal so that they get rid of this dangerous superstition from their heads as soon as possible.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Eventyret om skipsnissen gaar igjen blant mannskapet. Jeg har hoert om tilfeller der mannskapet hisset seg saa opp at hele skipet kom i fare. Jeg skal vaere strengere mot matrosene enn vanlig, saa de snarest faar denne farlige overtroen ut av hodet.

Styrmannen paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

Some of the older sailors are telling the younger ones, that the ship's kobold leaves all ships whose shipping line does not deal in a god fearing way. I was able to put aside the on setting restlessness among the crew, by telling them that you are the most honest trader in the entire Hanse. Everyone is now concentrating on their work on board.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Noen av de eldre sjoefolkene forteller de yngre at skipsnissen forlater alle skip der rederen ikke handler gudfryktig. Jeg kunne dempe den begynnende uroen blant mannskapet ved aa si at De er den aerligste handelsmannen i hele Hansaen. Alle konsentrerer seg naa om arbeidet om bord.

Styrmannen paa {%s:09}

column2:
{%7:00},

The passenger that we took on board in {%t:01} and were supposed to be taking to {%t:0A} has disappeared! I've had the crew scour the ship from the keel to the crow's nest, but there was no trace of him to be found anywhere.

Helmsman of the {%s:06}

column3:
{%7:00},

Passasjeren vi tok om bord i {%t:01} og skulle bringe til {%t:0A}, er forsvunnet! Jeg har latt mannskapet gjennomsoeke skipet fra kjoelen til utkikkstoennen, men det var ikke spor av ham noe sted.

Styrmannen paa {%s:06}

column2:
{%7:00}{%N:07},

Thank you for your help. Please obtain the following goods for me and get them to {%t:05}, in good condition and within 20 days:

{%B:09}{%w:10}
{%B:0A}{%w:11}
{%B:0B}{%w:12}
{%B:0C}{%w:13}
{%B:0D}{%w:14}
{%B:0E}{%w:15}

Store the goods there, in your trading office. I will have them collected at the given time.

{%V:16} {%N:06}

column3:
{%7:00}{%N:07},

Takk for hjelpen. Vennligst skaff meg foelgende varer og bring dem til {%t:05} i god stand og innen 20 dager:

{%B:09}{%w:10}
{%B:0A}{%w:11}
{%B:0B}{%w:12}
{%B:0C}{%w:13}
{%B:0D}{%w:14}
{%B:0E}{%w:15}

Lagre varene der, i Deres kontor. Jeg lar dem hente til avtalt tid.

{%V:16} {%N:06}

column2:
Estate of Mr Jakob Blank

Last night, Mr Jakob Blank died of natural causes in his {%t:09} home. He does not leave any descendants, and his recently amended will and testament names the {%R:00} Leopold Jantzen as his sole heir. An examination of his estate reveals that Jakob Blank, who ended his days living in impoverished circumstances, had a promissory note in the amount of 500,000\C.
The full amount will be sent to you forthwith.

The Town Treasurer, {%t:09}
{%+:09}

column3:
Doedsbo etter herr Jakob Blank

I natt doede herr Jakob Blank en naturlig doed i sitt hus i {%t:09}. Han etterlater ingen etterkommere, og hans nylig endrede testamente utpeker {%R:00} Leopold Jantzen som eneste arving. Gjennomgangen av boet viser at Jakob Blank, som endte sine dager i fattigdom, eide et gjeldsbrev paa 500 000\C.
Hele beloepet vil bli sendt til Dem uten opphold.

Kemneren i {%t:09}
{%+:09}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Last time we came ashore in {%t:07}, the crew was sitting in the inn as usual when some drunken sailor started bellowing stories about the Kobold around the room. He talked about his last ship, which was taken by the Kobold, and how he was the only person that managed to escape. You know, I don't set much store by these myths, but your crew has been on tenterhooks ever since. I have the situation under control and simply wanted to let you know.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Sist vi gikk i land i {%t:07}, satt mannskapet som vanlig paa vertshuset da en full sjoemann begynte aa broele historier om skipsnissen utover rommet. Han fortalte om sitt siste skip, som skipsnissen hadde tatt, og om hvordan han var den eneste som slapp unna. De vet at jeg ikke gir mye for slike myter, men mannskapet Deres har sittet som paa naaler siden. Jeg har situasjonen under kontroll og ville bare gi Dem beskjed.

Styrmannen paa {%s:04}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Strange sightings have been reported near {%t:07}. Several sailors have claimed on separate occasions that they have seen a ghost ship gliding through the waves under full sail, even though there was no wind. When they heard this, the crew's hearts sank, but they bravely continued with their duties. I have assigned twice as many guards as usual in an attempt to stop them worrying.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Det er meldt om merkelige syn naer {%t:07}. Flere sjoemenn har ved ulike anledninger paastaatt at de har sett et spoekelsesskip gli over boelgene for fulle seil, enda det var vindstille. Da mannskapet hoerte dette, sank motet, men de fortsatte tappert med arbeidet. Jeg har satt opp dobbelt saa mange vakter som vanlig for aa proeve aa berolige dem.

Styrmannen paa {%s:04}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

The cowardly rabble has fled. While we have been here in {%t:08}, every sailor except me has jumped ship for fear of the Kobold. You will have to enlist a new crew before we can set sail again, whether you want to or not.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Det feige paket har flyktet. Mens vi laa her i {%t:08}, har hver eneste sjoemann unntatt meg roemt av frykt for skipsnissen. Enten De vil eller ikke, maa De hyre et nytt mannskap foer vi kan sette seil igjen.

Styrmannen paa {%s:04}

column2:
Most esteemed {%R:01} {%n:01},

As we can see from Rostock, you certainly don't stint on your deeds. So we hope you will accept another sum by way of thanks, which you can invest in the town's further improvement right away. This time it is {%c:00}.

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Hoeyt aerede {%R:01} {%n:01},

Som vi kan se i Rostock, sparer De sannelig ikke paa Deres gjerninger. Derfor haaper vi at De vil ta imot enda et beloep som takk, som De straks kan investere i byens videre oppsving. Denne gangen er det {%c:00}.

Oldermannen {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
Worthy {%R:01} {%n:01},

You have not betrayed our confidence in you at all - on the contrary: Stettin is positively flourishing. So please take these {%c:00} for your future projects. This gold was donated by wealthy former traders to the Hanseatic League to be used for whatever purpose you wish.

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Verdige {%R:01} {%n:01},

De har slett ikke sviktet vaar tillit, tvert imot: Stettin blomstrer for alvor. Ta derfor imot disse {%c:00} til Deres fremtidige prosjekter. Dette gullet er gitt til Hansaen av rike tidligere handelsmenn, til bruk for ethvert formaal De oensker.

Oldermannen {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
Welcome, {%R:01} {%n:01},

Stockholm has once again become a magnificent town and we have you to thank for this. Take these {%c:00} as a token of our appreciation.

Your Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Velkommen, {%R:01} {%n:01},

Stockholm har igjen blitt en praktfull by, og det har vi Dem aa takke for. Ta imot disse {%c:00} som et tegn paa vaar takknemlighet.

Deres olderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

So I've been waiting and waiting and still no sign of my daughter? I was certainly wrong about you. Fine, I'll try and find her myself. I still have some hope.

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Jeg venter og venter, og fortsatt ikke spor av datteren min? Jeg tok sannelig feil av Dem. Greit, saa proever jeg aa finne henne selv. Jeg har ennaa litt haap.

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

This is the end for me! The last pleasure in my life has been sunk with that pirate {%N:06}'s cog! How could you have let that happen? May this deed be an onerous burden on your conscience forever!

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Dette er min undergang! Den siste gleden i mitt liv har sunket med piraten {%N:06}s kogge! Hvordan kunne De la det skje? Maatte denne gjerningen for alltid tynge Deres samvittighet!

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column2:
To all long distance traders!

Arsonists have turned our town into a flaming inferno, and we are very short of raw materials for rebuilding it. In order to increase our supplies of iron goods and bricks, previously stored fur stocks are being offered at reasonable prices in the market square.

Mayor of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Til alle fjernhandlere!

Brannstiftere har forvandlet byen vaar til et flammehav, og vi mangler saart raavarer til gjenoppbyggingen. For aa oeke beholdningene vaare av jernvarer og murstein tilbys lagrede pelsbeholdninger til rimelige priser paa torget.

Borgermesteren i {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
{%R:01} {%n:01},

I need your help! The wells in my town have been contaminated and now there is a plague raging relentlessly through the streets. I know you've already done a lot for my friends and me, but I beg you just to keep an eye on things, so that my lovely town is still well provided for.

Mayor of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
{%R:01} {%n:01},

Jeg trenger Deres hjelp! Broennene i byen min er forurenset, og naa herjer pesten naadeloest i gatene. Jeg vet at De allerede har gjort mye for vennene mine og meg, men jeg ber Dem bare holde et oeye med tingene, saa den vakre byen min fortsatt er godt forsynt.

Borgermesteren i {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Dear {%R:01} {%n:01},
The upturn of the Hanseatic League is complete! How can we ever thank you enough? You have saved the Hanseatic League and given new powers to the community. The townspeople will never forget you!

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:0D}

column3:
Kjaere {%R:01} {%n:01},
Hansaens oppsving er fullfoert! Hvordan kan vi noensinne takke Dem nok? De har reddet Hansaen og gitt fellesskapet nye krefter. Borgerne vil aldri glemme Dem!

Oldermannen {%F:00}{%+:0D}

column2:
Dear {%R:06} {%n:06},

Not very long ago, a terrible plague afflicted our town. Could you help us to rebuild London again? You will receive a handsome sum as payment if London can attract 1,000 new permanent residents and be restored to its former splendour.

The Mayor of London{%+:01}

column3:
Kjaere {%R:06} {%n:06},

For ikke saa lenge siden rammet en fryktelig pest byen vaar. Kunne De hjelpe oss med aa bygge opp London igjen? De faar en pen sum i betaling hvis London kan trekke til seg 1 000 nye faste innbyggere og gjenvinne sin tidligere prakt.

Borgermesteren i London{%+:01}

column2:
Dear {%R:06} {%n:06},

Thank you for helping us to rebuild London again. By way of thanks, I have had several deliveries of surplus wool brought to your trading office in Rostock.

The Mayor of London{%+:01}

column3:
Kjaere {%R:06} {%n:06},

Takk for at De hjalp oss med aa bygge opp London igjen. Som takk har jeg latt flere leveranser overskuddsull bringe til Deres kontor i Rostock.

Borgermesteren i London{%+:01}

column2:
Our saviour, {%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

What a wonderful blessing - you have liberated Stettin from the evil pirate. Now the long distance traders can put in at our town again without fear. Be assured of our eternal gratitude. We cannot give you gold, but we will reward you by filling your trading office with barrels of beer.

Mayor of Stettin{%+:03}

column3:
Vaar redningsmann, {%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

For en vidunderlig velsignelse: De har befridd Stettin fra den onde piraten. Naa kan fjernhandlerne igjen anloepe byen vaar uten frykt. Vaer forvisset om vaar evige takknemlighet. Gull kan vi ikke gi Dem, men vi beloenner Dem ved aa fylle kontoret Deres med toenner oel.

Borgermesteren i Stettin{%+:03}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

The pirate outside Stettin has not been seen again and only the Kobold himself knows what could have happened. But that isn't our problem, and we are hoping with all our hearts that the pirate will stay missing.

Mayor of Stettin{%+:03}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Piraten utenfor Stettin er ikke sett igjen, og bare skipsnissen selv vet hva som kan ha skjedd. Men det er ikke vaart problem, og vi haaper av hele vaart hjerte at piraten forblir borte.

Borgermesteren i Stettin{%+:03}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

It has come to our attention that some of the Dutch King's saboteurs have settled in {%t:01}. They probably want to prevent the Hanseatic League regaining its former position of power. Keep an eye on your stocks of goods! As soon as we know where these miscreants are lurking, we will contact you again.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Kjaere {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Det er kommet oss for oere at noen av den hollandske kongens sabotoerer har slaatt seg ned i {%t:01}. De vil trolig hindre Hansaen i aa gjenvinne sin tidligere maktposisjon. Hold oeye med varelagrene Deres! Saa snart vi vet hvor disse skurkene holder til, kontakter vi Dem igjen.

Hansaens raad{%+:05}

column2:
To all traders from Rostock,

An underhand act of sabotage destroyed all of the town's grain stocks as well as those belonging to some traders today. A search for the culprits is currently underway.

The Mayor{%+:01}

column3:
Til alle handelsmenn fra Rostock,

En lumsk sabotasje oedela i dag alle byens kornlagre og ogsaa lagrene til noen handelsmenn. Det letes for tiden etter gjerningsmennene.

Borgermesteren{%+:01}

column2:
To all traders from Rostock,

The saboteurs have struck again.

The Mayor{%+:01}

column3:
Til alle handelsmenn fra Rostock,

Sabotoerene har slaatt til igjen.

Borgermesteren{%+:01}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Our suspicions were right. It seems that the mayor of Bruges was coerced into the wicked acts by a councillor called {%N:0A} with forged documents. The councillor himself was commissioned by the Dutch King to worm his way into the mayor's confidence, with a view to weakening the Hanseatic League through piracy and sabotage. As far as we can tell, the mayor of Bruges is not to blame at all, however the corrupt {%N:0A} has escaped.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Kjaere {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Mistanken vaar var riktig. Det ser ut til at borgermesteren i Bruges ble tvunget til de onde gjerningene med forfalskede dokumenter av en raadsherre ved navn {%N:0A}. Raadsherren hadde selv faatt i oppdrag av den hollandske kongen aa innynde seg hos borgermesteren, for aa svekke Hansaen med sjoeroeveri og sabotasje. Saa vidt vi kan se, har borgermesteren i Bruges ingen skyld, men den korrupte {%N:0A} har sluppet unna.

Hansaens raad{%+:05}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Thank goodness! It is over! {%N:0A}, the wicked Dutchman, has finally been destroyed! Now the oceans and towns are safer places again and nothing else can stand in the way of the Hanseatic League's growth.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Kjaere {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Gudskjelov! Det er over! {%N:0A}, den onde hollenderen, er endelig tilintetgjort! Naa er havene og byene igjen tryggere, og ingenting staar lenger i veien for Hansaens vekst.

Hansaens raad{%+:05}

column2:
{%7:03},

Last time we came ashore in {%t:07}, the crew was sitting in the inn as usual when some drunken sailor started bellowing stories about the Kobold around the room. He talked about his last ship, which was taken by the Kobold, and how he was the only person that managed to escape. You know, I don't set much store by these myths, but your crew has been on tenterhooks ever since. I have the situation under control and simply wanted to let you know.

