That cowardly rabble has fled. While we have been here in {%t:08}, every sailor except me has jumped ship for fear of the Kobold. You will have to enlist a new crew before we can set sail again, whether you want to or not.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03},

Det feige paket har flyktet. Mens vi laa her i {%t:08}, har hver eneste sjoemann unntatt meg roemt av frykt for skipsnissen. Enten De vil eller ikke, maa De hyre et nytt mannskap foer vi kan sette seil igjen.

Styrmannen paa {%s:04}

column2:
Greetings,

The problems that we assigned you to deal with have been resolved. Our friends have urged us to settle the conflict in a peaceful, civilised manner.

{%N:09}

column3:
Vaer hilset,

Problemene vi ga Dem i oppdrag aa loese, er loest. Vennene vaare har oppfordret oss til aa bilegge konflikten paa en fredelig og sivilisert maate.

{%N:09}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Your ship, {%s:05}, is riddled with barnacles. This means that the condition of your ship is much worse than previously thought.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Deres skip {%s:05} er fullt av rur. Det betyr at skipets tilstand er langt verre enn antatt.

Havnefogden i {%t:07}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

It has come to our attention that the planks on your ship, {%s:05}, are in a much worse condition than previously thought. You are therefore strongly advised to have your ship repaired.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Vi har faatt vite at plankene paa Deres skip {%s:05} er i langt daarligere stand enn antatt. Vi raader Dem derfor sterkt til aa faa skipet reparert.

Havnefogden i {%t:07}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

It has been ascertained that the damage to your ship, {%s:05}, is much more serious than previously thought. It is in your own interests that we advise you to have the ship repaired as soon as possible.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Det er fastslaatt at skadene paa Deres skip {%s:05} er langt alvorligere enn antatt. I Deres egen interesse raader vi Dem til aa faa skipet reparert saa snart som mulig.

Havnefogden i {%t:07}

column2:
The pirate has been killed, but not by one of your ships!
So you are hardly entitled to the reward I promised you.

{%V:08} {%N:07}

column3:
Piraten er drept, men ikke av et av Deres skip!
Saa De har neppe krav paa beloenningen jeg lovet Dem.

{%V:08} {%N:07}

column2:
Hear ye! Oh Hear ye, citizens!

Tidings of our peaceful town's success have spread far beyond the city limits. Now despicable evil forces are plotting against our interests, demanding that we hand over the merchandise that we have worked so hard to produce. It is coming to our attention that a huge army of mercenaries will soon be coming to inundate us with murder, fire and looting.
We need to take precautions quickly to protect our homes, for we suspect there will be no way of averting this bloodthirsty assault.

The town of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Hoer, hoer, borgere!

Ryktet om vaar fredelige bys fremgang har spredt seg langt utenfor bygrensen. Naa smir foraktelige onde makter renker mot vaare interesser og krever at vi utleverer varene vi saa moeysommelig har produsert. Det har kommet oss for oere at en veldig haer av leiesoldater snart vil oversvoemme oss med mord, brann og plyndring.
Vi maa raskt ta forholdsregler for aa beskytte hjemmene vaare, for vi frykter at dette blodtoerstige angrepet ikke kan avverges.

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Citizens of {%t:04}!

Hordes of marauding mercenaries are sweeping through the land, leaving murder and pillage in their wake. No atrocity is beyond them. Who knows whether our prayers will be answered, so that they may leave our beautiful town alone?
So prepare yourselves, fortify the walls and stand by your arms.
May the walls and our courage hold!

The town of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Borgere i {%t:04}!

Horder av plyndrende leiesoldater drar gjennom landet og etterlater mord og plyndring. Ingen grusomhet er dem fremmed. Hvem vet om boennene vaare blir hoert, saa de lar vaar vakre by vaere i fred?
Gjoer Dem derfor klare, befest murene og hold vaapnene parat.
Maatte murene og motet vaart holde!

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Our gruelling business in {%t:08} is now complete.
I trust this has not tried your patience too much, and I would be grateful if you would now take me to {%t:00}.

Courier on board the {%s:05}

column3:
Vaare slitsomme forretninger i {%t:08} er naa avsluttet.
Jeg haaper dette ikke har satt Deres taalmodighet altfor mye paa proeve, og jeg ville vaere takknemlig om De naa foerte meg til {%t:00}.

Kureren om bord paa {%s:05}

column2:
Dear Sir or Madam,

The Hanseatic League is delighted to announce that a race will be taking place on {%D:01} between the Hanseatic League's boldest traders!
The voyage begins in {%t:15} and takes the participants to {%t:18}. Curious onlookers are more than welcome to attend the race.
The following traders are taking part in the race:

{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02}
{%R:03} {%v:03} {%n:03}
{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}
{%R:05} {%v:05} {%n:05}
{%R:06} {%v:06} {%n:06}
{%R:07} {%v:07} {%n:07}
{%R:08} {%v:08} {%n:08}
{%R:09} {%v:09} {%n:09}

The wagers have been collected from all participating Traders. They must arrive on the {%t:15} with their competing ships. 
The fastest ships will then run the race at dawn on the {%D:01}. 

May the fastest ship win!

The Court of the Hanse!

{%+:12}

column3:
Kjaere herre eller frue,

Hansaen har gleden av aa kunngjoere at det den {%D:01} holdes en kappseilas mellom Hansaens dristigste handelsmenn!
Reisen begynner i {%t:15} og foerer deltakerne til {%t:18}. Nysgjerrige tilskuere er mer enn velkomne.
Foelgende handelsmenn deltar i kappseilasen:

{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02}
{%R:03} {%v:03} {%n:03}
{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}
{%R:05} {%v:05} {%n:05}
{%R:06} {%v:06} {%n:06}
{%R:07} {%v:07} {%n:07}
{%R:08} {%v:08} {%n:08}
{%R:09} {%v:09} {%n:09}

Innsatsene er krevd inn fra alle deltakende handelsmenn. De maa moete i {%t:15} med sine kappseilasskip.
De raskeste skipene seiler saa kappseilasen ved daggry den {%D:01}.

Maatte det raskeste skipet vinne!

Hansaens domstol!

{%+:12}

column2:
Hoist the sails!

The race has begun.
The line-up consists of the following contestants:

{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02} {%s:1B}
{%R:03} {%v:03} {%n:03} {%s:1C}
